<title>HONG KONG: China Pharma 1996 net rises 71 percent.</title>
<headline>China Pharma 1996 net rises 71 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   5.5    vs 3.2</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.2    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    33.15  vs 19.39</p>
<p>    Turnover		     211.96 vs 106.93</p>
<p>    Company name		 China Pharmaceutical Enterprise</p>
<p>				     and Investment Corp Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 2-6</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 23</p>
<p>NOTE - China Pharmaceutical Enterprise is a China-backed Vitamin C maker.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 2.4 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 1.2 cents) vs 1.4 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
